    },
    {
      "id": "claim_56b270a4a14246ec9263b76a788dfc5e",
      "statement": "When using function calling (tool calls) instead of raw text output, JsonOutputToolsParser and PydanticToolsParser extract and validate the structured data from tool call arguments. PydanticToolsParser validates parsed tool arguments against Pydantic schemas and raises ValidationError if validation fails, supporting first_tool_only mode to extract a single structured output.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/output_parsers/openai_tools.py#L139-L350",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5669c169d4d9dd26ccaadbea957eac3a492777611f47c450f992dac26317f291:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b536363906a14d3fb260de6b698f2bc2",
      "statement": "The agent framework provides specialized error types for structured output via tool strategies: StructuredOutputValidationError is raised when tool arguments fail schema validation, and MultipleStructuredOutputsError when the model returns multiple tool calls when only one is expected. These errors carry the ai_message and can trigger retries with error context sent back to the model.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/structured_output.py#L35-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8a131eadf9d5ee730ba0931b207fbc4b94a030a9d1751356e9549880dbceb0f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_047babb4f82b4299baa42a7dc281101f",
      "statement": "_SchemaSpec is a dataclass that encapsulates a structured output schema (Pydantic model, dataclass, TypedDict, or JSON schema dict) along with its name, description, strictness, and derived JSON schema. It normalizes all schema types through schema_kind classification and extracts json_schema for both tool binding and provider strategy use.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/structured_output.py#L106-L193",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97b580993fe9832e499db71338047965638ba04d553de9b102698fabb6d87952:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_392ec5e12c7f480fb55eeb23b1177078",
      "statement": "ToolStrategy enforces structured output via artificial tool calls by wrapping schemas as StructuredTools and parsing arguments using TypeAdapter validation. It supports Union types and handle_errors for automatic retry on validation failure. ProviderStrategy uses provider-native structured output by converting schemas to JSON Schema and binding model kwargs. Both strategies parse results through _parse_with_schema() and store in structured_response.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/structured_output.py#L195-L315",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb3d222146832b851f2342bc182199346552b002177c1df3af6e67756cef49d0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/structured_output.py#L318-L431",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:93f2cebce855ae732d61be0fafe80b54514f3b9f74e8c6bc0d3a73afef9e4aef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9c1961c376c54b62b7591017c5f3dd7e",
      "statement": "AutoStrategy defers structured output strategy selection to runtime, checking model capabilities via _supports_provider_strategy() at invocation time. If the model supports provider-native structured output (detected via profile metadata or fallback patterns), it uses ProviderStrategy; otherwise, it falls back to ToolStrategy. This enables portable agents that use optimal strategy per model.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/langchain_v1/langchain/agents/factory.py#L1399-L1422",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8eb3cd2199100151783cc5bf9e74fb0a1bf4f6069b23486988c940c376a16d53:"
